                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_199">Evesham,
                        Worcestershire. Benedictine abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St Egwin</orgName><p>'Liber Abbathie (?) de Euesham 2o fo Galathis' (fol. iii verso,
                        opposite first leaf of text; 'hie' and the second 'b' of the second word
                        seem certain).</p><p>Evesham ex-libris legible by ultra-violet
                        light.</p><p>Probably a staple chain mark at foot of last leaf: the mark are
                        clearer by u-v. light.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Magdalen pressmark 'E pa' and title 'Epistole
                     Senece' (s. xv) on fol. iii verso.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Caucio M. E. Albo[n ?] exposita ciste sancti
                     Johannis 28 die nouembris 1470 . . .' with three supplements, St Thomas on the
                     Sentences 2o fo tens(?) tunc(?), Chrysostom on Pauline Epistles 2o fo [ . . .
                     ], and Sermones G[ . . . ], 2o fo [. . .]', mainly legible by u-v. light -- on
                     verso of last leaf. 'xxs' at head of last verso.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">This was a Cambridge chest. No doubt E.
                     Albon, fellow of Gonville Hall.</provenance>
